teach_motor.description:
Selected device: {selected_blind}
Command/transmit identity: {command_device_id}/{command_enum}

Optional: before sending, select the device's channel on an already paired original remote control, press its programming button until the channel LED blinks, and then press Stop. Home Assistant sends the teach-in command 60, waits for the stick's ACK confirmation, sends the finish command 40 on the same enum value, and then performs a short Up/Stop test on the device. The stick's ACK confirmations do not prove that the device has learned the teach-in code enum 60 or has moved. Do not repeat command 60 outside the motor programming sequence; it can also change the direction of rotation.

send_raw_command.description:
Selected device: {selected_blind}
Configured enum: {command_enum}

Enter exactly 11 characters: ss + two-digit enum + repeat digit + two-digit command + 0000. Example: ss109010000. Commands are 00 Stop, 01 Up/Open, 02 Down/Close, 40 Finish/Allow Pairing, and 60 Teach-in/Change Direction. t1/t0 only confirms the transmission cycle of the stick.
